The '''Mayor of Sant Cristòfor''' ({{lang|ca|Alcalde de Sant Cristòfor}}) is the elected head of the municipal government of [[Sant Cristòfor]], the capital of [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. The mayor serves as the city's chief executive, with authority over municipal administration, planning, and major infrastructure. The mayor serves four-year terms with a two-term limit, and is elected by direct popular vote.

The current mayor is [[Oriol Cardona i Ousmane]] of the [[Socialist Front of Balboa]] (FSB), who took office in 2025 following a snap election triggered by the arrest of his predecessor, [[Núria Gomila i Renom]] (BPP), in a financial crimes investigation.

== History ==

=== First Republic (1854–1899) ===

{{main|First Republic of Balboa}}

The office of mayor was established at independence in 1854. The municipal government during the First Republic was dominated by a succession of mayors who were almost without exception deeply corrupt and in the pocket of business interests. The mayor's office was effectively an extension of the city's commercial elite: merchants, railway company agents, Zong trading houses, and the owners of the salt works and shipyards all competed for influence over the municipal administration. Mayors were selected not by the electorate but by the commercial factions that dominated the city council.

The most dramatic event of the period was the assassination of Mayor [[Joan Ballester i Forteza]] on the steps of the [[Sant Cristòfor Grand Train Terminal]] in 1886 by a disgruntled former municipal employee. The last mayor of the First Republic, [[Pere Gomila i Sastre]], fled the city ahead of Zong forces in 1899.

