=== Zong Balboa period (1899–1950) ===

{{main|Zong Balboa}}

The Zong administration abolished the elected mayoralty. The city was placed under the authority of the Zong governor, who appointed a [[Grand Administrator]] (Zong: 總行政官) to manage the city. The Grand Administrator was unelected and answered directly to the governor. Each ciutat had its own local council, but these were advisory bodies with no executive power.

