=== Post-mandate period (1960–present) ===

{{main|Politics of Balboa}}

The return to Balboan sovereignty in 1960 re-established the mayoralty under the Balboan constitutional framework. The [[Balboan People's Party]] (BPP) dominated the mayoralty from 1960 through the 1980s, reflecting its support among the Black working-class majority. The [[Liberal Party of Balboa|Liberal Party]] won the mayoralty in the 1980s, reflecting the growing influence of the professional and commercial classes. From 2000 onward, the mayoralty alternated between the BPP and the Liberals until the 2025 snap election, in which the [[Socialist Front of Balboa]] (FSB) won for the first time.

The mayor serves four-year terms with a two-term limit (8 years maximum). The current mayor, [[Oriol Cardona i Ousmane]], was elected in a snap election following the arrest of his predecessor.

